  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishing DNA-based Monitoring of an Asian Elephant population in Kuiburi National Park, Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to, (1) Collect fecal-DNA samples and conduct capture-mark-recapture analysis to estimate a baseline Asian elephant population in Kuiburi National Park; Fecal DNA will be analyzed in Nepal; (2) Facilitate the adaptive management of Asian elephant conservation activities within Kuiburi National Park through providing a robust Asian elephant population estimate against which the effectiveness of conservation interventions within, and around, the protected area can be measured; (3) Promote fecal DNA capture-mark-recapture analysis as the primary framework for Asian elephant monitoring in the Dawna Tennaserim Landscape through production and dissemination of a minimum of two conservation resources: a Thai language manual and a peer-reviewed scientific publication.</narrative>
  </description>
